<p>USFans country spreadsheet — UK/NL/US are separate documents.</p>
  <p>USFans spreadsheets are country documents. The .net host is the US/global desk and stays untouched. .uk, .co.uk and .nl are live local sheets — they must not 301 onto .net.</p>
  <p>Quote after packed kg, then pick a line that actually hands off to Royal Mail or a tax-prepaid product — not a screenshot from a US blog.</p>
  
  <p>USFans on the .uk hostname is a separate United Kingdom spreadsheet/desk from any .co.uk twin. Nominet .uk is its own URL: Royal Mail Tracked product names after packed kg, in GBP. Do not 301 .uk onto .co.uk or onto a .net doorway.</p>
  <h2>Country spreadsheet — line cards for this last-mile only</h2>
  <p>Singular spreadsheet: the live line card and warehouse-photo notes for this country’s last-mile. It is not a dump of every SKU in a shared catalog and not the agent’s marketing homepage. If a bare ccTLD exists, that host handles account signup; this one handles packed-kg comparison.</p>
  <p>A 2.4 kg hoodie haul that hands off to Royal Mail is a different SKU from the same clothes on an untracked 500 g tee line. Read the product name in the agent app after the warehouse photo, not a US blog screenshot.</p>
  <p>UK import rules and any VAT/duty are set by HMRC and the carrier product you buy. This page does not pick a declared value for you.</p>
